00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.380
The practical method is to set a clear extension rule such as adding only after the first

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:19.540
tranche shows a 5% gain and volume exceeds the 20-day average. Then use the same options chain

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:24.720
or limit order ladder already in your brokerage. This tactic has historically worked best

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.140
in trending sectors during earning season when initial beats attract follow-on institutional flow.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:35.860
It carries the risk of overexposure if the catalyst fades before the second tranche is added.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.920
Retail investors can implement it immediately on platforms like Questrade or Interactive Brokers

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.860
by using staged limit orders tied to volume alerts. The key is treating the second entry as an

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:53.780
extension of proven strength, not an attempt to average down. This is the exact scenario where our

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.760
earlier rule about volume confirmation would have helped avoid the healthcare launch loss we

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:04.800
