00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:36.110
Imagine you hold a Canadian bank ETF in your TFSA and the Bank of Canada announces it is holding

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:44.290
the policy rate at 2.25% with no change to forward guidance. Your order fills at the 10 AM ET

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:52.290
open, yet the ETF drifts another 0.8% lower by noon, even though the headline decision matched expectations.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:58.130
The mechanism is the press conference itself. Governor McLembe's tone on inflation

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:03.490
persistence and the exact wording around data dependent decisions often shifts the yield curve

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:10.410
more than the rate decision. Bit asks spreads on rate sensitive ETFs can widen from 3 cents to 12 cents

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:17.650
in the first 45 minutes. What most retail investors do not realize is that the 2.30 pm fed press conference

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:24.350
next week will similarly move the entire TSX financial sector regardless of the FOMC dot plot.

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:30.750
The Q&amp;A reveals the committee's reaction function to incoming PCE data. The biggest mistake

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:36.090
with central bank events is assuming the rate decision is the only tradable output. Instead,

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:41.250
always wait for the first 30 minutes of the press conference before adding or trimming rate sensitive

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.370
positions so you can see whether the language tightens or eases relative to the statement.

